<title>NORWAY: DnB 9-month profits rise.</title>
<headline>DnB 9-month profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>				   (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income	     3,171     vs	  3,188</p>
<p> Net other operating income    2,095     vs	  2,036</p>
<p> Total operating expenses	3,357     vs	  3,493</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p> losses				1,909     vs	  1,730</p>
<p>Net reversals on loans</p>
<p> and guarantees			303     vs	    374</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating profit	2,219     vs	  2,104</p>
<p> Net profit			  2,202     vs	  2,092</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's biggest commercial bank is Den norske Bank ASA. Eight analysts polled by Reuters had forecast a nine-month net profit of 2,070 million crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
